Falsifies `paging::nth_allocation::a_failed_map_range_leaks_no_table`.

The defect: the same "atomic" unwind as the `map_block` record, in `map`: on `OutOfPageFrames`
it clears the first table entry this call installed, orphaning every table below it. `map_range`
calls `map` once per page, so a range that fails on its second page after its first page built the
tables leaks the tables the failing page built.

Expected to fail: assertion (1), "table frame(s) handed out and unreachable from the root", at
`map_range` with allocation 1 failed. The other three tests in the file go red too, because every
path reaches `map`; this record names the one it was written for.

Replay by hand, because `script/falsifications` sweeps Kani harnesses and kernel `#[test_case]`s
and this is a host `#[test]`; it is reported as a known gap, not as rot:

    git apply crates/paging/falsifications/nth_allocation.a_failed_map_range_leaks_no_table.patch
    cargo test -p paging --test nth_allocation a_failed_map_range_leaks_no_table        # must fail
    git apply -R crates/paging/falsifications/nth_allocation.a_failed_map_range_leaks_no_table.patch

Run on 2026-10-04 (UTC), patagonia: red as predicted, green again after the revert.

